Subject: [PATCH 6/6] R80b, part 4, patch 6 (cld-advisor, at main's word in
 M14; Review 80, the SM seat's finding 40, WHICH MAIN HAS NOT CHECKED: it was
 made again before it was mended): THE CARD OF AN ARC ID THAT SEVERAL FOLDERS
 CARRY SHOWS EVERY FOLDER.

THE FINDING, MADE AGAIN by running the query. One id, B58, is carried by three folders, one of them RETRACTED. Its card read the first folder's verdict file and no other: it printed that verdict under the name the atlas keeps, which is another folder's, and the retracted folder never appeared.

WHAT IS CHANGED. Every folder that carries the id is on the card, each with its own verdict and claim line. The head carries every verdict, and says that several folders carry the id and that the atlas keeps one name for them. For an id with one folder the card reads as it did. The function returns each folder's verdict as well; the one key "verdict" is empty where there is more than one.

THE TEST holds the card of B58 to the three folders' own verdict files, counts that B58 is the one shared id on the tree, and holds a twin with one folder. With the query of the commit before it fails. The atlas's tests: 15 pass. 0 of 19.
